  "description": "German and continental scholarly transliteration: one sign per letter and no digraphs (ṯ ǧ ḥ ḫ ḏ š ṣ ḍ ṭ ẓ ġ), ʿ (U+02BF) for ʿayn and ʾ (U+02BE) for hamza, article with sun-letter assimilation (aš-Šams), ى = ā, ة = h (t in construct).",
  "sources": [
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DIN_31635",
    "https://itftennis.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/1272938619/Passport%20Standards.pdf?api=v2",
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romanization_of_Arabic"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Word-initial hamza is not written (DMG practice: Aḥmad, Ibrāhīm); medial and final hamza are ʾ.",
    "Sources disagree on ة: English Wikipedia (and the research notes) give -h / -t in construct; German Wikipedia gives -a / -at (DMG usage). This file follows -h; construct-state -t and case endings are not generated (pausal forms).",
    "Final nisba -iyy is written ī; medial -iyy- is kept doubled (-iyyah). Nunation is ignored.",
    "After a word ending in a vowel the article loses its a (Abū l-Wafāʾ), implemented as a post-processing step; the DMG shortening of the preceding long vowel (Abu l-) is not applied.",
    "The DIN text itself (paywalled) was not consulted; values come from the research notes, ICAO Doc 9303 Part 3 App. B and Wikipedia."
  ],
